# Agent Auto Selection

- For every user request, first check project agents in `.agent/agents/`.
- Never wait for a user reminder like "use an agent" if a matching specialist is available.
- Match task intent to the best agent profile (frontend, backend, qa, security, docs, etc.).
- Prefer the narrowest specialist that fits the task; use orchestrator only for multi-domain work.
- If multiple specialties are needed, run multiple agents in parallel and merge results.
- If no suitable agent exists, continue with direct execution and state that fallback was used.
- For renderer/UI tasks (`electron/renderer`, HTML, CSS, responsiveness), default to `frontend-specialist`.
